# /etc/tmpfiles.d/w2c.conf — the PLATFORM's directories on this box, made at every boot whoever starts first.
# Installed and applied by install-obsd.sh (`systemd-tmpfiles --create`), beside `vms.conf` (the VMS's directories).
# ================================================================================================
# NOTES — what every part of this file does and why (kept beside the code, not in a separate document)
# ================================================================================================
# # w2c.tmpfiles — the platform's state, its configuration, its secrets and the console's door
#
# **Role.** The platform is w2c and the VMS one of its subsystems (the product's rule, 3 October), and the box's
# directories split the same way: what every process of the platform needs is here, what the VMS's processes need is
# in `vms.tmpfiles`. The product's pair is `/etc/tmpfiles.d/w2c.conf` (its `/var/lib/w2c`, `/run/configstore`) and
# `vms.conf`; the course's box keeps its state on the data partition (М9 Lesson 5), so its paths are under /data —
# ALL the platform's mutable state under one root, `/data/platform` (the owner's decisions, 4 October), and its
# configuration with it: /etc/w2c is a link to `/data/platform/etc`, which `install-obsd.sh` lays (an A/B box's /etc
# is on the slot an update replaces).
#
# - `/data/platform` — `PLATFORM_DIR` (`w2c.env`), root's: nothing writes in it but the directories below.
# - `etc/` — this box's `/etc/w2c`: `w2c.env` (root's, 0644), and in a cluster `configstore-rights.json` and `tls/`.
# - `etc/secrets` — the cluster's key ring, `platform.key` (`python3 -m w2cplatform.sealing new
#   /etc/w2c/secrets/platform.key`: 0640). 2710 root:`w2c-secrets`: the members of the group — the console, the
#   holder, the recorder — may pass through to the file they are told, and not list what else is there (`x`
#   without `r`); setgid, so a key made here is the group's without a `chgrp`; root alone writes it, because no
#   running process does. Mounted, as one file, into the three units that open sealed fields and nowhere else; and
#   no unit mounts `/data/platform` whole, only the stores below — a copy of a store must not carry the key.
# - `config/`, `objects/` — the platform's two file stores (`file://`): the rows, and the heartbeats and the snapshot.
#   2770 `w2c`:`w2c-store`, setgid: every unit opens them as a member of `w2c-store` with the umask 0007, so a row
#   or an object any process writes is a file the resource — `w2c`, not root — reads, and the rows' lock one it takes.
# - `events/` — the platform's events archive (`RESOURCE_ROOT`), the resource's: 2770 `w2c`:`w2c-events`, setgid. A
#   process that writes buckets is a CLIENT, a member of `w2c-events` with the umask 0007: what it makes there is
#   0660 in directories 2770 of the group, which the resource deletes by its retention. Only the resource deletes buckets,
#   mirrors and restores there.
# - `/run/w2c-console` — the console's unix socket, the box's own door (`CONSOLE_UNIX`, `console.container`; the
#   review's sixth pass). The console is the platform's process (ADR 0014), so its directory is here. 0700 root, and
#   the socket in it 0660 — who may open it is this mode, which is the point of it. A directory of its own and not
#   one under /run/vms: that one is mounted whole into the holder's and the recorder's containers, and the console's
#   door is not theirs to open.
#
# `d` sets the mode and the owner of the directory itself at every boot; what is inside — a box upgraded from root's
# `/data/archive` — is handed over once, by `install-obsd.sh`, not at every boot.
# ================================================================================================
d /data/platform              0755 root root        -
d /data/platform/etc          0755 root root        -
d /data/platform/etc/secrets  2710 root w2c-secrets -
d /data/platform/config       2770 w2c  w2c-store   -
d /data/platform/objects      2770 w2c  w2c-store   -
d /data/platform/events       2770 w2c  w2c-events  -
d /run/w2c-console            0700 root root        -
